# t2_consensus_r8_20261103: PREREG_R8_CHANGES (changes before T_c and before any round-8 evaluation)

**When.** 2026-11-02, from about 21:25 to 21:50 CST. This is before T_c = 2026-11-03 12:00:00 CST and before any
round-8 export, evaluation, score or selection. The orchestrator had not been launched, and no `POOL_R8.*` existed.

**Why.** An independent review of the first locked build found problems in crash-recovery paths and in what the frozen
records would copy from Zuxing's files. This revision applies its fixes. Every change either leaves the selection rule
unchanged, or brings the code and the text back to what PREREG_R8 already stated or what round 7 did.

**First build (superseded, kept read-only in `superseded_build1/`):**
- `PREREG_R8.md` 3293d704f8d12c7f3d7a5c1b12330a96407dd467732bdc8f461c5aeadb1974b7
- `PREREG_R8_PINS.md` af4523be3998d2e51a8d5b3d8f2a79bff335659482f9d53393b718197607917a
- `LOCK_R8.sha256` 39537deecbcb6db742d0acf401f4e871b2c5055070bb391e757594c7dca7c5a2
- `DRYRUN_R8.md` 25bfb7b122d644f79b731b5fe2d0b62236ebb7967a7ff51c2e60a886975d6398

Its trial pool folders were deleted (plumbing only, never used by a decision). The document in force is the
`PREREG_R8.md` whose sha256 the round-8 scripts hard-code; `LOCK_R8.sha256` lists it.

## 1. Changes to the text of PREREG_R8.md

| section | change | kind |
|---|---|---|
| When | records this revision and `superseded_build1/` | record |
| Basis, 2.6 (2) | the watcher header must hold the 8 asserted columns and no column outside the watcher's 18-column own-input header, else the freeze stops (before: the 8 columns had to be present; other columns were not checked) | stricter check, fail-safe |
| Standing rules, 2.6 (2), 2.8 | record copies of Zuxing's text files hold only what round 8 uses: MANIFEST.txt keeps its run / source / copied / status / train log / task.parquet / parquet sha256 / models / files lines; checksum files keep the lines of model, rsi, final.json, training-log, MANIFEST.txt and hydra files; the watcher record copy keeps the 8 asserted columns; any text line that round 7's token guard refuses is left out; a training-log line it refuses keeps only its commit. Full-source sha256 before / after stay in `COPIES_r8.tsv`. Checkpoints are always byte copies | records only; nothing that the selection reads changes |
| C1, 2.6 (5) | on a 5090-hosted run, the watcher's last ok-evaluated iteration counts off the 10,000 grid only when it is also the run's last counted iteration L. C1 already stated that D2 "has the same restriction" (grid + the run's last iteration); the code did not enforce it when a 5090 watcher stopped before the end of its run. At the development dry run of 21:39 this changes no pick (6 of the 20 5090 watcher rows have last ok != L; none of their picks is off the grid) | correction: code brought to the stated C1 |
| C6, 7.1 | the scorer's gate / score steps answer "already done" when their verified output exists, so a relaunch resumes (7.1 already said every step is resumable) | correction: code brought to 7.1 |
| 7.4 | a pin / preflight / integrity failure of the evaluation driver halts (before: it was retried 6 times and phase S then ended as keep-r7, unlike what 7.4 said); after 6 failed restarts phase F halts (before: it wrote `DEADLINE_F.json`, which the scorer's check would refuse, so it halted anyway at the next step); a phase-F deadline passed while no evaluation driver runs halts at the scorer's check | correction: code and text aligned; every such path leaves the R7 file in force |
| 7.6 (new) | one evaluation driver at a time: the orchestrator never starts `r8_eval.py` while one is alive (read from /proc, nothing signalled) and never counts that wait as a restart; keep-r7 and the scorer refuse while one is alive; a stale `driver.pid` of an ended process does not count; `r8_launch.sh` refuses to start while one is alive | fixes a relaunch that could end round 8 as keep-r7 while evaluations still ran |
| 8 | budget from the development dry run of 21:39 (89 new screen candidates in 24 episodes) | record |
| 9.2 | what the reviser saw | disclosure |
| 10 | this file is part of B4 and of `LOCK_R8.sha256` | record |

Unchanged: T_c, the universe and eligibility, R1-R5, D1-D5, C2-C5, the incumbents and bars, the evaluation protocol,
GPUs 6/7 only while no other compute process is listed, the phase-S and phase-F rules, the closest-to-mean trial, the
phase-S cut-off (2026-11-04 08:00 CST) and the phase-F deadline (2026-11-04 12:00 CST).

## 2. Changes to the scripts

- `r8_pool.py`: `zguard` applies round 7's token guard to every path in Zuxing's folder before its allowlist (for a
  watcher file, to its `eval_<ep>` directory, because round 7's list names that file); exact watcher-header check;
  record excerpts (`copy_meta`, `watcher_excerpt`); the 5090 condition of 2.6 (5); `WATCHER_R8.tsv` gains the columns
  `pruned_host` and `last_ok_counts_off_grid`.
- `r8_driver.py`: `live_evals` (/proc only), no second `r8_eval.py`, waits not counted as restarts, liveness instead of
  `driver.pid` existence at a deadline, `halted` on a pin / preflight / integrity failure, phase F halts after 6 failed
  restarts.
- `r8_select.py`: `driver_running` counts only live `r8_eval.py run` processes (not a plan-only `--dry-run`),
  `pidfile_live` replaces the `driver.pid` existence test, keep-r7 refuses while an evaluation driver is alive, gate /
  score "already done" when their verified output exists.
- `r8_launch.sh`: refuses while an `r8_eval.py run` process is alive.
- `r8_eval.py`: only its hard-coded PREREG_R8 sha256.
- `dryrun/r8_mock_select.py`: three added checks (keep-r7 refused while an evaluation driver is alive; no live one
  now).

Off-server simulations of the orchestrator (stubbed processes, clock and /proc: earlier evaluation driver still running,
stale `driver.pid` at a deadline, preflight failure, pinned-file mismatch, repeated crash, `halted` heartbeat, deadline
during a run, crash then success) and of gate / score resumption gave the intended result in every case. Steps B2-B4
were then re-run with the final scripts (`DRYRUN_R8.md`).
